# virtio-snd over virtio-uml: the guest gets a real ALSA card.
#
# The device is instantiated from the kernel command line with
#   virtio_uml.device=<socket path>:25     (25 = VIRTIO_ID_SOUND)
# and the host end is the app-side backend (app/audio/vusnd.c), a vhost-user
# device that plays the PCM into Android's AAudio.
#
# Gates, checked on this tree:
#   - SOUND depends on HAS_IOMEM || INDIRECT_IOMEM. UML defaults to
#     NO_IOMEM=y; UML_IOMEM_EMULATION selects INDIRECT_IOMEM and clears it
#     (the same gate the fbdev/DRM fragments open).
#   - The stock fragments leave `# CONFIG_SOUND is not set`; nothing selects
#     SOUND back on, so both levels are explicit here.
#   - SND_VIRTIO selects SND_PCM and SND_JACK. No hardware card driver is
#     needed: the virtio device *is* the card.
#   - SND_PCM_TIMER stays at its default (y); ALSA's hw-pointer/period timer
#     is what the virtio-snd driver's elapsed_period work relies on.
CONFIG_UML_IOMEM_EMULATION=y
CONFIG_SOUND=y
CONFIG_SND=y
CONFIG_SND_PCM=y
CONFIG_SND_VIRTIO=y
